{# FLASHES — one markup, rendered once, by the frame.

   Before the shell, the host rendered these one way and two modules
   rendered them two other ways, each with its own class and its own tick glyph,
   so "saved" read differently depending on which screen you came from. The
   frame now says it, above the body, in the platform's own plate.

   The label is carried in a data attribute rather than baked into a class list,
   so a deployment can restyle a kind of message without the shell enumerating
   the kinds — the label vocabulary is the application's, not the layout's. #}
{%- if flashes|length > 0 -%}
    <div class="flashes">
        {%- for label, messages in flashes -%}
            {%- for message in messages -%}
                <div class="c" data-shell-flash="{{ label }}">{{ message }}</div>
            {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
{%- endif -%}
